Leave the SDK case overlays out of a toolchain that runs on Windows.

The MSVC toolchain adds two overlays, which let a case-sensitive exec file system resolve the mixed-case file
names of the Windows SDK: `-ivfsoverlay` for the headers, `/vfsoverlay` for the libraries.
`//tools/case_insensitive_vfs` builds them, and it is a `stage1_hosted` C binary. On a Windows exec host,
that binary resolves the same Windows MSVC toolchain, whose arguments need the overlays again, so analysis
fails with a dependency cycle through `@bazel_tools//tools/cpp:link_extra_lib`.

A Windows file system is case-insensitive, so such a toolchain does not need the overlays. Move both into a
`case_overlays` list, and add it only when the exec OS is not Windows.
